      "writtenOn": "2026-07-12T18:20:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 1331: Behavioural change for non-call request types in the extension. Previously iOSConnectedCb_ was consulted for *every* request type on iOS (`if (iOSConnectedCb_(connType, peer_h)) return;`). Now it is gated behind deferMessageDedup, which requires connType \u003d\u003d videoCall/audioCall. So for any other connType (file transfer, sip, generic sync, etc.) the extension will no longer invoke iOSConnectedCb_ and will instead process the request itself via onDhtPeerRequest and mark it treated — consuming it from the main app. If the callback was also used to hand non-call connections to the main app, this is a regression. Please confirm the extension is only ever expected to short-circuit audio/video call requests; if other types must also defer to the main app, the connType filter is too narrow.",
      "revId": "6d276b6e1cfd3d95c78351838528e6d9442ccb3d",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
