      "writtenOn": "2026-07-12T18:20:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 1339: Reservation leak on the untrusted / cert-not-found path. When deferMessageDedup is true the id has already been inserted into transientIOSCallRequests_ by reserveIOSCallRequest(), but this else branch (foundPeerDevice() \u003d\u003d false) never calls finalizeIOSCallRequest() nor otherwise erases the id. Consequences: (1) For a genuine peer whose *first* findCertificate() returns null transiently (cert not yet fetched), the id stays reserved, so every subsequent DHT re-announcement of that same call request is dropped by reserveIOSCallRequest() returning false — the call can never ring on retry. (2) The id lingers until FIFO-eviction at 1024 entries. Please erase the reservation here on failure, e.g. add `if (deferMessageDedup) shared-\u003etransientIOSCallRequests_.erase(req.id);` (under messageMutex_, or via a small releaseIOSCallRequest() helper) in the else branch. The same fix must be mirrored in the second (non-legacy) handler\u0027s else branch.",
      "revId": "6d276b6e1cfd3d95c78351838528e6d9442ccb3d",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
