      "writtenOn": "2026-07-12T18:20:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 1898: Eviction policy evicts the numerically-smallest id, not the oldest reservation. transientIOSCallRequests_ is a std::set\u003cdht::Value::Id\u003e ordered by id value, so erase(begin()) removes the lowest id regardless of when it was inserted. Under a flood this can evict a still-in-flight reservation whose async findCertificate() has not yet completed; a concurrent duplicate of that request would then be re-reserved and could double-signal CallKit — defeating the dedup this code exists to provide. Consider a FIFO structure (e.g. a std::deque\u003cValue::Id\u003e for order plus the set for lookup, or a ring buffer) so eviction drops the oldest entry, and ideally avoid evicting ids that are still pending certificate resolution.",
      "revId": "6d276b6e1cfd3d95c78351838528e6d9442ccb3d",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
